WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
This is The Spread, your energy
markets briefing for Tuesday,

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.680
the tenth of November. This episode
is written and read with AI.

3
00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:12.080
Qatar's prime minister is taking an
Iranian proposal to reopen the Strait

4
00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:17.040
of Hormuz to the White House, and Brent
fell about seven percent on Monday.

5
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.720
That came on the same day Saudi
Arabia's main pipeline around the strait

6
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:21.920
was attacked.

7
00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:26.520
On the markets. Brent fell to ninety-four
dollars a barrel by early Monday,

8
00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:31.040
and WTI to eighty-eight dollars
ten, according to OilPrice dot com.

9
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:34.880
By the close, Brent's loss on the
day had reached about seven percent,

10
00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.480
after a sixteen percent slide last week.

11
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:41.813
European gas storage was seventy-two
point four percent full as of Sunday,

12
00:00:41.947 --> 00:00:45.600
according to Gas Infrastructure
Europe, and US distillate stocks stood

13
00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:49.120
at about ninety-nine point three million
barrels in the week to the thirtieth

14
00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:51.680
of October, according to the EIA.

15
00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.467
Starting with the diplomacy.

16
00:00:53.493 --> 00:00:56.880
The Qatari prime minister was heading
to Washington with Iranian terms

17
00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:01.240
for an interim deal to reopen the
strait, OilPrice dot com reported.

18
00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:05.120
Two diplomatic sources told Israeli
media that Tehran has signed off

19
00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:10.320
on those terms. Separately, Al Arabiya
cited unnamed sources saying Washington

20
00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:14.533
would let Iran enrich uranium to
just under three point seven percent,

21
00:01:14.587 --> 00:01:17.840
under a mediation track
run by Qatar and Pakistan.

22
00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:19.547
None of this is confirmed.

23
00:01:19.573 --> 00:01:23.600
The accounts are one-sided or unsourced,
and neither government has confirmed

24
00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:27.867
any terms. President Trump said only
that further strikes depend on a

25
00:01:27.973 --> 00:01:31.600
very strong agreement, which
signals no new attacks for now.

26
00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:35.880
Secretary of State Rubio called
Tehran's demands so far unacceptable,

27
00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:37.240
Rigzone reported.

28
00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:41.040
Even so, crude traders are pricing
the Hormuz risk premium out of the

29
00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:43.680
market before anything changes physically.

30
00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:45.560
And flows are still tight.

31
00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:49.920
According to the EIA, US imports of
Iraqi crude are at their lowest since

32
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.600
the two thousand and three war,
falling to zero in several weeks over

33
00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:57.200
the summer. Iraq's foreign minister
puts the country's war losses at

34
00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:00.520
about sixty billion dollars,
according to Al Jazeera.

35
00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:04.160
To Saudi Arabia, where the East-West
pipeline was attacked in the Medina

36
00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:08.000
region on Monday. An Energy Ministry
official said the attack caused

37
00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:12.080
a limited fire, which was put out,
with no casualties and no disruption

38
00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:15.627
to operations. The line
feeds Yanbu on the Red Sea,

39
00:02:15.653 --> 00:02:19.160
the port that handled most of the
kingdom's export growth in October.

40
00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.240
If the official's account holds, the
route around Hormuz is still working.

41
00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:27.360
But the attack puts that main
bypass directly in the line of fire.

42
00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:31.440
Separately, a Houthi attack damaged
an Aramco tower in Riyadh's financial

43
00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:33.440
district, Rigzone reported.

44
00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:37.680
And a Reuters survey put OPEC output
back at ninety percent of its pre-war

45
00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:38.480
rate.

46
00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:42.080
In the strait itself, tankers
were set ablaze over the weekend,

47
00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:45.120
and the US military bombed
a bulk carrier on Saturday,

48
00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:47.280
according to Splash twenty-four seven.

49
00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:51.280
Iran issued fresh mine warnings, and
explosions were reported along its

50
00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:55.760
southern coast. Apart from the US strike,
no one has been named as responsible

51
00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:56.560
for any of it.

52
00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:00.480
Turning to diesel. Two tankers
carrying Russian diesel,

53
00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:05.040
the Talisman and the Leruo, have turned
away from their declared US destinations

54
00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:08.880
after loading at Primorsk in
October, OilPrice dot com reported.

55
00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.880
A third is in the North Atlantic
with no declared discharge port.

56
00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:16.720
The Treasury has authorised Russian
diesel transactions under the President's

57
00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:19.360
arrangement with Putin. Lawmakers, though,

58
00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:22.560
warn that importers could still
breach a congressional ban.

59
00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:25.360
That legal risk is keeping
the barrels from landing,

60
00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:29.280
so US distillate buyers get no
relief from this route for now.

61
00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:33.520
Over to gas. Liquefied natural gas
is trading above thirty dollars per

62
00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:36.400
million British thermal
units going into winter,

63
00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:39.840
and Europe holds its lowest gas
inventory of the twenty-twenties,

64
00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:41.840
according to OilPrice dot com.

65
00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:45.600
China is pulling back from spot
buying, as cheap domestic supply and

66
00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:47.520
inventory releases kick in.

67
00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:51.040
Bloomberg reported China's national
average price at about twenty-two

68
00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:54.960
dollars, almost ten dollars
below the Japan Korea Marker.

69
00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:58.640
Weaker Chinese bidding could leave
more spot cargoes for Europe.

70
00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:03.040
The catch is demand. Cloudy weather
pushed European peak power prices

71
00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:05.840
to their highest since
twenty twenty-two on Monday,

72
00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:10.560
which lifted gas burn. Low wind is
expected to last until at least midweek,

73
00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:14.480
so gas-fired generators and the
utilities buying their power are carrying

74
00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.320
the cost.

75
00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:16.480
A few more things.

76
00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:20.800
Hungary's MOL reported third-quarter
net profit of about eight hundred

77
00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:24.640
and sixty-five million dollars, up
around a hundred and forty percent

78
00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:28.560
on the year, on strong refining
margins, according to Rigzone.

79
00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:32.480
In the Black Sea, war-risk insurance
premiums have reached twenty percent

80
00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:36.240
of hull value after Russia claimed
more strikes on merchant ships,

81
00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:38.320
Splash twenty-four seven reported.

82
00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:42.080
The US Office of Foreign Assets
Control issued an update to its Iran

83
00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:45.600
sanctions designations. The
summary doesn't give details.

84
00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:49.840
Leaked letters suggest Iran used
Chinese terminals to keep sanctioned

85
00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:54.720
tankers moving. So far only Iran
International has reported this.

86
00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:59.120
Strathcona agreed to buy Greenfire
for up to two point one billion US

87
00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:03.600
dollars. The deal creates Canada's
fourth-largest steam-assisted gravity

88
00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:06.160
drainage operator in the oil sands.

89
00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:11.440
And COSCO Shipping Energy has lined up
twenty-four very large crude carriers.

90
00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:15.760
Ten of them are newbuilds, worth
about one point four billion dollars.

91
00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:20.080
What to watch next. Today, the
Senate votes on the bipartisan energy

92
00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:23.280
permitting bill, which now
has the President's backing.

93
00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:27.760
On Wednesday, the EIA weekly report
covers the week to the sixth of November,

94
00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:30.400
and distillate stocks are
the figure to look for.

95
00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:34.320
Daily readings on EU gas storage
continue through the sixteenth.

96
00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:38.320
And the Jones Act emergency
waiver expires on the fifteenth.

97
00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:42.080
That's the brief. Sources for everything
you heard are in the show notes.
